The exact Steiner DP is already strong for small destination sets. The main opportunity is the large-broadcast fallback: its greedy incremental tree can be worse than simply taking the union of independently cheapest source-to-destination paths. Build both feasible broadcast trees and select the one with lower unique-edge cost. This preserves path validity while avoiding unnecessary relay edges.

Also explicitly assign empty paths when `src` appears in `dsts`, since the source already has the data and should not be left with `None` partition paths.

